#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0119 expect=noViolation domain=CO
#note "ESCALATE -- do not re-aim: this fixture deliberately pins an UNDER-REPORT and is the evidence for the M3-D22 relabel. There is only ONE COVAL column and its single cell holds a 250-character comment that was never split at all -- exactly the sheet's Condition, 'Comment value > 200 characters in length'. With fewer than two series members evalColumnSeriesMetadata returns FALSE before either test runs, so the rule is silent. That is why 'Fully Executable' was wrong: what the rule actually verifies is that an EXISTING split is well formed. M3-D22 moved this rule's Executability from 'Fully Executable' to 'Partially Executable - Possible Underreporting' with no Check change: column_series_metadata reads only DECLARED column lengths and never a data cell, so the sheet's Condition ('Comment value > 200 characters in length') cannot be detected on an unsplit comment. Reading the data would need a length-of-value operator the engine does not have."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#expectViolationCount 0
dataset CO label="Comments"
col STUDYID type=Char length=12 label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char length=2  label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char length=20 label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col COSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col COVAL   type=Char length=200 label="Comment"
---
S1 | CO | 001 | 1 | xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
---
